  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 760310,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## Advanced Dungeons & Dragons: Heroes of the Lance (Commodore Amiga)\n\nEmbark on a thrilling quest inspired by the beloved Dragonlance fantasy world in *Advanced Dungeons & Dragons: Heroes of the Lance* for the Commodore Amiga! This 1988 action-adventure game faithfully adapts the \"Dragons of Despair\" campaign module and the first Dragonlance novel, *Dragons of Autumn Twilight*.\n\nPlayers control a succession of eight heroes, each with unique abilities – including healing magic, wizardry, and trap removal – as they navigate challenging side-scrolling levels. A unique gameplay mechanic sees heroes appearing to replace fallen comrades, adding a strategic layer as you manage your party's survival.  The game utilizes authentic Dungeons & Dragons statistics, bringing the tabletop experience to life on your Amiga.\n\nWhile praised for its impressive graphics and audio upon release, be warned: *Heroes of the Lance* is known for its punishing difficulty and lack of save functionality.  Prepare for a demanding but rewarding adventure, steeped in classic D&D lore!"
    },
